Dump reader utilities

Helper: /usr/local/bin/dump-reader help

This image reads existing regular files only. It can inspect metadata, compute
SHA-256 checksums, and copy a selected file to a separate output mount. It
does not generate dumps or alter source files. Copy-out is limited to 1 GiB,
stays beneath /input and /output, and never overwrites an existing file.

Read the runbook before use:
/usr/share/dump-reader/RUNBOOK.md
README: /usr/share/dump-reader/README.md
